                <pb facs="0404" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Legation in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-11T16:00:00-00:44">July 11, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>33. Department’s telegram 13, June 22, 2 p.m. Barber Line representative,
                    Monrovia, states that to date he has not received any instructions from his
                    principals and there have been no shipments on his vessels since May 14th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
